docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:99:Token age (days:hours, with the Sunday cadence marked), last successful sync per feed, recent job failures, API spend this month. One control: **Pause system** (kill switch): stops all proposal creation and submission until unpaused. Unpause requires typed confirmation.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:104:- **Stale data:** any market number older than its cache window shows a staleness mark with timestamp. Never render a price without its age being discoverable.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:106:- **Empty states:** pre-first-sync dashboard, empty journal, empty queue each need a designed state (the queue's empty state is the normal state most of the time).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:110:Push (deep-link only, no figures in the payload): new proposal, fill/cancel, halt tripped, unprotected position, token expiring. Email: morning brief, EOD summary, Sunday ritual, job-failure digests. Original list:
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:112:- Morning brief (07:00), EOD summary (16:30), Sunday ritual
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:115:- Guardrail halt tripped
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:116:- Token expiring (T-24h), escalations Mon/Tue if Sunday re-auth missed
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:121:- No live-updating tickers or streaming charts. Numbers refresh on load and on Turbo-stream events (fills, sync completions). This is a decision system, not a terminal.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:122:- No P&L celebration/loss states. The journal treats +2R and −1R rows identically.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:130:- **Transactions table → Journal browser.** Summary strip (net change / in / out) above a dense table with Data Views, Filters, Date, Keywords, Amount as inline dropdowns, group-by rows with expand chevrons. Direct lift for journal: R this month / wins / losses strip, then trades with setup filter as the first dropdown.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:140:- **Midday (web) → app shell and dashboard.** Icon-only collapsed left rail (~40px) with a top search bar; dark theme; chart cards with a headline number, legend (current / previous / average), dashed average line, and a timeframe dropdown plus "Customize" at the card row's top right. Layout: one full-width primary chart, then a 2-up row of smaller chart cards. Our mapping: equity curve as the primary chart with HWM as the dashed line; the 2-up row is open risk over time and drawdown from HWM. The rail holds our five areas: dashboard, proposals, journal, watchlist, system.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:141:- **Mercury (web) → detail panel, journal table, confirm pattern.** Unchanged from the section above: right-hand slide-over for proposal detail, transactions table for the journal, authorization-line-above-one-button for Approve, inline "similar item exists" callout for warn and reconciliation states.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:142:- **Copilot Money (web), supplemental.** Three cards worth lifting: "Transactions to review" with its reviewed-everything empty state (our proposal queue on the dashboard), the range-chip row (1W / 1M / 3M / YTD / 1Y / ALL) on the net-worth chart, and "Next two weeks" as a dated upcoming list (our earnings/econ events touching the book).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:143:- **Mobile supplements (iOS).** Revolut Business approval detail for the proposal screen structure; Navan's in-policy / out-of-policy idiom for pass/warn/fail rows and the override-with-reason sentence; Life Reset's Quick Add for the journal entry.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:145:Open interaction with the earlier question: a dark shell makes "halt mutes the whole palette" a weaker signal than on a light UI; the halt banner probably has to carry the state on its own.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:151:- **Benchmark overlay on the performance chart.** Legend row of portfolio vs S&P 500 vs component ETFs, each with its return, and a hover tooltip comparing "your portfolio" against the benchmark on a given date. Lift for the dashboard equity curve (portfolio vs SPY), and it doubles as the visual for the allocation module's correlation check.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:152:- **Holding detail page.** Price chart with range chips, a "Your position" strip (balance, shares, cost basis, return, allocation), then a right-column card with News / About tabs and a stats row below. This is our **Position detail** screen, which the inventory above omits. Our version of the strip: shares, cost basis, unrealized P&L, working stop, distance to stop, this position's share of open risk. Right column tabs become Thesis (from the originating proposal) and History (journal legs for this instrument).
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:155:- **"Pro view" toggle** on the holdings table: a dense-mode switch for the journal browser.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:160:**Monarch** is not on Mobbin. Worth screenshotting directly for the board: its transactions "needs review" queue and the net worth / holdings views are the closest consumer analogues to our proposal queue and dashboard.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:162:Screen inventory addition: **Position detail** (mobile + desktop), reached from any position row on the dashboard.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:170:**Guardrail headroom as budget bars.** Budget card rows (label, planned amount right-aligned, progress bar, spent left / remaining right in green). Direct lift for a "Risk budget" card on the dashboard: risk-per-trade used, daily loss used vs halt threshold, sector exposure vs cap, concurrent positions vs max. Remaining headroom in green; the bar goes to the warn color as it approaches the cap. This makes the guardrail engine visible before a proposal trips it.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:172:**Review modal → orphan-fill and incomplete-journal review.** "Is this merchant recurring? There are 9 more to review": entity card with recent transactions, a few form fields, and three actions (Skip / Not recurring / Save as recurring). Ours: "Is this fill part of a setup? N more to review", recent fills for the instrument, setup dropdown and planned stop, actions Skip / Not a trade / Save. The orange top banner with "Review now" is the pending-review entry point; the nav badge count (Recurring 10) is the proposals count on the rail.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:178:**Cash Flow analytics → journal analytics.** Segmented Monthly / Quarterly / Yearly, paired positive/negative bars per period with a net line and a dashed projection for the current period, then four stat tiles. Ours: winning R / losing R bars per period, expectancy line, tiles for net R, win rate, avg winner, avg loser. Skip the Sankey.
docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:182:**Also worth keeping:** "Your Weekly Recap · date range" card as the in-app entry to the Sunday review; "this month vs last year" comparison line for equity vs prior period; Recurring's "in 1 day" countdown for upcoming earnings/econ events and "settles Tue".
docs/phase-1-plan.md:1:# Phase 1 Plan: Investment Copilot (read-only)
docs/phase-1-plan.md:3:Source of truth: `docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md` (v9). Screen states from `docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md` and the wireframes. This plan covers only PRD §6 Phase 1 as scoped in the kickoff brief. Revision 2 incorporates the counselors PRD review (codex-5.5-high, claude-fable; outputs in `agents/counselors/1788296923-*`).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:5:Sections: decisions, migrations, jobs, tool surface, journal builder, stops and open risk, snapshots, UI, testing, deploy, build order, deferred items, Schwab assumptions, working method.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:15:5. **`evaluate_hypothetical_order` omitted** from Phase 1. `get_risk_rules` ships and returns the (empty) `risk_rules` rows.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:26:| # | Table | Key columns | Phase 1 populated? |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:37:| 10 | `activities` (the PRD's `transactions`; renamed because `transaction` is reserved by Active Record) | One row per Schwab activity. `account_id`, `instrument_id` (nullable for cash-only), `order_id` (FK, nullable), `broker_order_id` (nullable), `broker_activity_id` (unique per account), `kind` enum (fill, sweep, dividend, interest, fee, deposit, withdrawal, transfer, corporate_action, other), `status` (Schwab's VALID/INVALID/PENDING; only VALID is journaled), `sub_type` string (raw Schwab type), `side`, `quantity`, `price`, `commission`, `fees` (summed from the activity's fee transfer items), `net_amount`, `trade_date`, `settlement_date`, `executed_at`, `raw` jsonb, `journaled_at` | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:39:| 12 | `trades` | `account_id`, `instrument_id`, `setup_id` (nullable), `order_proposal_id` (nullable), `status` enum (open, closed) only, with a partial unique index allowing one open trade per account and instrument, `needs_review` bool, `review_reason`, `excluded_from_stats` bool, `stopped_out` bool, `initial_quantity`, `total_risk` (orphan or bootstrapped, missing setup/stop), `bootstrapped` bool (created from an existing position, entry history unavailable), `opened_at` (nullable when bootstrapped), `closed_at`, `avg_entry`, `avg_exit`, `peak_quantity`, `planned_stop`, `planned_target`, `initial_risk`, `realized_pnl`, `realized_r`, `thesis`, `post_mortem`, `followed_setup` (nullable bool), `journal_completed_at` | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:43:| 16 | `audit_events` | `kind` string, `actor` enum (human/system/agent), `user_id` (nullable), `subject` polymorphic (nullable), `data` jsonb, `reason`, `created_at` only. Postgres triggers reject UPDATE, DELETE, and TRUNCATE; `kind` is validated against `AuditEvent::KINDS`. Reserved for the PRD's "logged" list; not telemetry. | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:46:| 19 | `agent_runs` | `kind` enum (morning_brief, eod, sunday_review), `status`, `degraded` bool (ran with expired token / stale data), `started_at`, `finished_at`, `tool_turns`, `input_tokens`, `output_tokens`, `estimated_cost`, `output_markdown`, `error`, `model` | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:48:| 21 | `system_settings` | Singleton row (check constraint `id = 1`): `shadow_mode` bool default true, `manual_halt` bool default false, `manual_halt_reason`, `manual_halt_at`, `sync_paused_reason` (set while token expired) | yes |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:58:**Token model (revised after the step 4 counselors review).** Pause state is *derived* from the current token, never written by a failure. `schwab_tokens` gains `revoked_at`; `SchwabToken.current` is the newest by `issued_at, id`; `usable?` = present, not refresh-expired (`issued_at + 168.hours`, elapsed time not calendar days), not revoked. `SchwabToken.issue!(response)` inserts the new row and clears `system_settings.sync_paused_reason` in one transaction, enqueuing `Sync::CatchUpJob` after commit. `SchwabToken#refresh!` takes the row lock, reloads, and returns early if the row is no longer current or was refreshed in the last minute (so two workers cannot double-refresh and a stale row cannot act); it builds the client inside the lock; `access_expires_at` = now + `expires_in` − 60 s; `refresh_token` = response value or the existing one; `refresh_expires_at` is never touched. On `ReauthRequired` it sets `revoked_at` on the current row only, records `last_refresh_error` outside the lock so a rollback cannot lose it, audits `token_refresh_failed`, and sets `sync_paused_reason`. On `ServerError`/`TransportError` it records the error and does nothing else. `ensure_fresh!(margin:)` refreshes proactively when the access token is near expiry, so a 401 is the safety net rather than the norm. `Schwab.client` raises `Schwab::NoUsableToken` rather than letting nil reach a request.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:60:**Token gating.** Only `Sync::TickJob` and the agent jobs are scheduled; everything else is enqueued by them. When `SchwabToken.current` is not usable, the tick job writes one `sync_runs` `skipped_token` row per hour, audits `sync_paused_token_expired` once per episode, and enqueues nothing. No self-re-enqueue, so the queue cannot grow. The re-auth callback (`issue!`) clears the pause, audits `sync_resumed`, and enqueues `Sync::CatchUpJob`, which runs all feeds with windows widened to cover the gap (capped at the 60-day limit). Agent jobs run degraded rather than wait: `degraded: true`, the prompt states the token is unusable and every number carries its as-of time, the email subject is prefixed, and the token status line sits at the top of every brief so a dead nag path is still visible daily. Snapshots are not written for days without a fresh balance.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:62:**Re-auth flow.** `SchwabController#authorize` (login required) stores a random `state` with a timestamp in the session and redirects to the authorize URL. `#callback` (login required; an unauthenticated hit is rejected without storing a return-to URL, so the code never lands in the session) reads and deletes the pending state; no pending state renders "nothing pending, start again" with no audit; a mismatch audits `re_auth_failed` as CSRF; `params[:error]` (user cancelled) renders the failure without calling the token endpoint. On success: `exchange_code`, then `/accounts/accountNumbers` must overlap the known `accounts` hashes (first auth accepts anything) or the token is not made current and `re_auth_failed` is audited; then `issue!`, audit `re_auth_succeeded`, and **redirect** to a clean success page so a browser refresh cannot resubmit the single-use code. A failed exchange never writes to `schwab_tokens`. The retry link goes to `authorize`. `code`, `state`, and `session` join `filter_parameters`. The callback URL comes only from `SCHWAB_CALLBACK_URL`, never from the request. `fake_authorize` 404s unless the adapter is fake and the environment is not production, and `?fail=1` redirects with a bad code for Playwright.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:64:**Health and nags.** `Schwab::TokenHealthJob` runs 08:00 and 20:00 ET. Nag when: no usable token (absent, revoked, or expired), sent at every run; or the 24-hour warning, sent once per token row (deduped on token id in the audit data). Monday/Tuesday escalation fires when `SchwabToken.current.issued_at` is before the most recent Sunday 18:00 ET, which is the PRD's literal "the Sunday re-auth hasn't happened"; no buffer, no comparison against the coming Sunday. Cron strings carry `America/New_York` explicitly. The refresh task gets a higher queue priority than sync.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:71:| `Sync::AccountsJob` | daily 06:05, after every re-auth | `/accounts/accountNumbers` only; upsert by `schwab_hash`. New accounts land with `trading_enabled: false` and no `account_type`; the system screen shows accounts needing operator setup |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:84:| `Agent::SundayReviewJob` | Sunday 18:00 | Phase 1 stub, no API call: re-auth link, token age, sync health, job failures, setup stats table |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:90:**Activity kinds.** TRADE with an EQUITY security → `fill`; TRADE with a CASH_EQUIVALENT security or MONEY_MARKET → `sweep`; DIVIDEND_OR_INTEREST → `dividend` when a security is present, else `interest`; ELECTRONIC_FUND, ACH_*, WIRE_*, CASH_* and JOURNAL with only currency items → `deposit` or `withdrawal` by sign; JOURNAL or RECEIVE_AND_DELIVER with one security → `transfer` (ACAT deliveries are not corporate actions), with two securities → `corporate_action`; all items fees → `fee`; anything else → `other` and counted. Activities whose `status` is not VALID are stored and never journaled.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:100:`app/models/agent/tools/*` each defines `name`, `description`, `input_schema`, `call(**args)`, and permission metadata: `read_only`, `interactive_allowed`, `scheduled_allowed`. The MCP server registers tools where `interactive_allowed`; the scheduled runtime passes only tools where `scheduled_allowed && read_only`, enforced in one place so a Phase 2 write tool cannot reach an unattended run by omission. Phase 1 tools:
docs/phase-1-plan.md:105:| `get_account_health` | Equity, settled/unsettled cash, drawdown from HWM (index-based), unprotected count, token status and age, last sync per feed, shadow mode, halt state, sync pause reason |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:106:| `get_quotes(symbols)` | Schwab `/marketdata/v1/quotes`, cached 2 min in Solid Cache, each quote stamped with fetched_at; when the token is expired returns the cached value with `stale: true` or an explicit unavailable error |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:108:| `get_journal(filters)` | Trades with legs; filters: status, needs_review, setup, instrument, date range, missing_post_mortem |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:110:| `get_risk_rules` | Active `risk_rules` rows (empty in Phase 1) |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:114:**MCP server:** `POST /mcp` (Streamable HTTP, JSON-RPC 2.0). `McpAuth` extracts a bearer from `Authorization` and compares with `ActiveSupport::SecurityUtils.secure_compare`; 401 renders a plain "MCP auth failed" page (Playwright target). See decision 0.8 for the OAuth fallback.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:116:**Scheduled runtime:** `Agent::Run` wraps one Messages API conversation: system prompt = memory repo markdown files + setup stats + token health + as-of timestamps; tools = scheduled-allowed registry; hard cap `MAX_TOOL_TURNS = 12`; result stored in `agent_runs` and emailed via `BriefMailer`. Prompts live in `app/models/agent/prompts/*.md.erb`. The morning-brief prompt states that earnings and economic-calendar data are unavailable in Phase 1 and must not be inferred. Morning brief and EOD are real; Sunday review stub does not call the API.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:122:IRA and other read-only accounts sync positions and activities (for Phase 2 wash-sale checks) but never create trades. `Journal::BootstrapJob` and `Journal::LinkFillsJob` share one Solid Queue concurrency key per account, and every activity is linked in its own transaction: insert or find the leg by `activity_id`, recompute the trade as a pure function of its legs, then stamp `journaled_at` last. A rerun finds the existing leg and recomputes; it never skips because the activity was marked.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:124:**Bootstrap** (`Journal::BootstrapJob`, after every complete positions sync). Every open position in a trading-enabled account has one open trade. Its synthetic `entry` leg is a **reconciling plug**: quantity = broker quantity − net quantity of the linked fill legs, priced at the broker average price, recomputed after every bootstrap and link run and deleted when it reaches zero. A trade whose plug is non-zero is `bootstrapped: true, needs_review: true, review_reason: bootstrapped`, with `opened_at` nil. Positions with zero quantity or no average price are skipped. After a complete positions sync, an open trade whose instrument has no position and no unjournaled fills is flagged `review_reason: position_missing`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:126:**Link fills** (`Journal::LinkFillsJob`), per account and instrument, VALID unjournaled activities in `executed_at, id` order:
docs/phase-1-plan.md:132:- A re-synced activity whose quantity, price, or status changed after journaling has its leg dropped and `journaled_at` cleared, then the instrument replays.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:133:- Dividend or interest on an instrument with an open trade: `income` leg (feeds realized P&L, not basis). After close, attach to the most recent closed trade on that instrument within 90 days and recompute; otherwise journal with no leg. Return of capital is treated as income in Phase 1.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:137:- Sweeps, deposits, withdrawals, fees, and cash-only transfers: `journaled_at` set, no leg.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:140:**R math.** `initial_quantity` = every entry fill sharing the first entry's `order_id` (fallback: all entries before the first exit), so a partial fill does not understate risk. `initial_risk` = `initial_quantity` × (average initial entry price − `planned_stop`), fixed once the stop is known; at or below zero it is nil and so is R. `realized_r` = `realized_pnl` / `initial_risk`. `total_risk` = sum over entry legs of quantity × (price − stop at that time), stored for the journal browser, never used as the R denominator. A bootstrapped trade closed before review takes setup and thesis only; its R stays nil.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:148:## 5. Stops and open risk in Phase 1
docs/phase-1-plan.md:157:- Portfolio open risk sums protected positions only, and the dashboard and `get_account_health` state how many positions are excluded and why.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:164:- `equity` = the latest balance at or after the regular close on that day, else the day's latest balance, else **no snapshot** (a stale balance is never smeared across days). The first snapshot is the first day with positive equity, with return 0 and index 1.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:170:Dashboard day change is flow-adjusted (equity − flows − prior snapshot equity) and reads "no prior snapshot" on a gap day. The EOD fills recap reads activities journaled today; the missing-post-mortem list excludes `needs_review` and `excluded_from_stats` trades.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:178:**Model prerequisites built in this step.** `SchwabToken.status` (missing, revoked, expired, expiring, missed_sunday, healthy) extracted from the health job and used by the banner, the system page, the mailer, and later `get_account_health`; `Account#sync_interval(feed)` and `Account#last_sync(feed)` extracted from the tick so views and scheduler cannot disagree; `trades.review_deferred_at` so Skip is durable ("later, not never": queue ordered by priority, then deferred-at nulls first, then oldest); `Position#distance_to_stop` guarded on a stop price rather than full protection so a partially covered stop still shows its distance; CASH_EQUIVALENT positions skipped by the positions sync so the sweep fund is neither a position nor a trade; `trading_enabled` requires `taxable`; an `account_configured` audit kind and an immediate sync enqueue when an account is enabled; setups creatable by name from the review form.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:180:| Screen | Route | Phase 1 content |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:182:| Dashboard | `/` | Banner by state: not connected (connect CTA); revoked (re-auth, with the refresh error); expired (re-auth, "sync paused since" from the first skipped run); expiring (re-auth, "Sunday's email will remind you" when covered); halted ("Halted by John, Mon 11:14a: reason. Clear it on the System page", no fake rule copy, re-auth link still shown if sync is also down); sync failed with a usable token (one-line status under the header, not a banner); needs setup (link to the accounts section). Equity with flow-adjusted change since the prior snapshot by date ("since Fri close" on a Monday, "first snapshot after today's close" before one exists); settled and unsettled cash ("unavailable", never zero, when both readings are nil); open risk labelled as known protected risk plus "N excluded: partial / oversized / awaiting / trailing / no stop"; positions as a list of rows sorted unprotected, awaiting, and trailing first then ascending distance, each with symbol, size, distance to stop as the primary number, the protection state inline, unrealized P&L (market value minus cost basis) second, and the older of the positions and orders as-of stamps; "N trades need review" callout; "Proposals: Phase 2" without a link; empty states for not connected, waiting for the first sync, and no open positions. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:184:| Trade detail / post-mortem | `/trades`, `/trades/:id` | List with needs-review and missing-post-mortem filters (the EOD email deep-links there); detail with legs, planned versus actual stop (working stop for open trades, closing price when stopped out), R; the Flow 4 quick entry: required one line plus followed or improvised |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:185:| System | `/system` | Token status and age against 7 days with next Sunday 18:00 marked and a loud line when the token dies before it; last success and latest status per feed per account, `gap_from` when set, pause reason and since; failed sync runs plus Solid Queue failed executions in 7 days; shadow mode as a read-only indicator; API spend rendered as "0 runs, briefs start in step 9"; memory repo "never"; accounts table showing each account's equity and top symbols with an inline form for nickname, type, and enabled. Halt: set requires a reason and audits `manual_halt_set`; clear requires typed confirmation checked server-side and audits `manual_halt_cleared`. One word everywhere: Halt. |
docs/phase-1-plan.md:189:**Staleness.** A broker-derived number is stale when it is older than twice the account's current sync interval for its feed plus the minute of slack, or whenever sync is paused. The orders as-of is the finish time of the latest advanced orders run. Quotes stale after 2 minutes, price history after 5, snapshots are close-of-day artifacts.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:193:Banner precedence: halted > revoked > expired > not connected > expiring > healthy, with a secondary status line for any other active condition. Halted in Phase 1 comes only from `system_settings.manual_halt`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:199:- **RSpec**, in the kickoff's priority order: token lifecycle with `travel_to` (25-minute refresh, 7-day expiry unaffected by refreshes, pause and catch-up, Mon/Tue escalation rule); sync jobs with fixture payloads (positions incl. removal, orders incl. cancel/replace and working stops, transactions incl. cash dividend, split, return of capital, CUSIP succession, fee items); journal linking (scale-in/out, orphan fill, sell-first legacy holding, bootstrap, ticker change on same CUSIP, R math); snapshot math (flows, late-landing deposit rebuild); MCP tool contracts (auth, each tool's schema and output, permission metadata excludes non-scheduled tools); scheduled runtime with a stubbed Messages API (turn cap, degraded mode).
docs/phase-1-plan.md:201:- **`Schwab::FakeClient`** implements the same interface as `Schwab::Client`, returns canned payloads, selected by `config.x.schwab.adapter`. Used by dev seeds and Playwright.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:202:- **Playwright** (`e2e/`, `@playwright/test` via npm, the only Node dependency): a scenarios route drawn only under `Rails.env.test?` and guarded again in the controller with `Schwab.fake?`, which resets the fake client, seeds with the factories (never by driving jobs), and signs in a seeded user by setting the session cookie because there is no inbox to read a magic link from. Times are relative: fresh is now, stale is three hours ago, expiring is 22 hours out, expired is two days ago. Scenarios: healthy, expiring, expired, halted, not connected, needs setup, one unprotected position, a failed sync with a usable token, the review queue with Skip persisting across reload, the post-mortem save, re-auth success and failure (the seeded hash must match the fake's), and the MCP 401 page (step 8). The Playwright server runs with the test queue adapter.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:203:- **`bin/ci`**: Rails 8.1 `ActiveSupport::ContinuousIntegration` with steps in `config/ci.rb`, the pattern borrowed from Patchvault. Kickoff order: rubocop → rspec → brakeman (strict, warnings fail) → `bin/importmap audit` → `bundle exec bundle-audit check --update` → Playwright (`bin/playwright`, which boots a test-env server with the FakeClient, runs `npx playwright test`, and tears down). Fails on the first red step.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:218:1. Tooling: RSpec, rubocop config, brakeman, bundler-audit, `bin/ci` (without Playwright), authentication generator adapted to magic link, AR encryption keys, credentials layout, crest in the layout.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:224:7. Dashboard, system health, trade screens; Playwright added to `bin/ci`.
docs/phase-1-plan.md:231:## 11. Explicitly not built in Phase 1
docs/phase-1-plan.md:266:Counselors runs are long (10 to 20 minutes) and run in the background while unrelated work continues. Whole-phase gates: the counselors PRD review before step 1 (done, revision 2 of this plan is the result), and a DHH pass plus counselors review over the full Phase 1 diff after step 10.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:1:# Step 7 design review: dashboard, system health, trade screens, Playwright
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:3:Based on the PRD §5.8 to §5.10, the flows doc, the wireframes, plan §2, §5, §6, §7, §8, and the models and jobs as they exist on disk today.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:9:**2. The money-market sweep fund is a position and a trade.** The account fixture holds SWVXX as a CASH_EQUIVALENT position with average price 1.0 (lib/schwab_fixtures/account.json:21). `Sync::PositionsJob` keeps every nonzero-quantity row (app/jobs/sync/positions_job.rb:13), `Journal::BootstrapJob` skips only zero quantity or nil average price (app/jobs/journal/bootstrap_job.rb:10), and `Position#protection` returns `:unprotected` for it. On the first real sync the dashboard shows a 2,110-share "unprotected" position, the unprotected count is off by one, open risk excludes it "with a reason," and a bootstrapped SWVXX trade for 2,110.5 shares sits at the top of the review queue. Filter CASH_EQUIVALENT at the positions sync, or at minimum skip it in bootstrap and in every dashboard query. Do it in the sync: the activity mapper already treats CASH_EQUIVALENT trades as sweeps, so the positions side should agree.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:11:**3. The banner treats "never connected" as "expired."** The design branches on `SchwabToken.usable?`, which is false with no row at all. First login shows "Token expired. Sync paused. Re-authenticate," and `Sync::TickJob#pause!` has already written a pause reason that says "re-authenticate" (app/jobs/sync/tick_job.rb:49). Revoked is a third distinct case: Schwab rejected the refresh, and the copy should say so with `last_refresh_error`. `Schwab::TokenHealthJob#nag_reason` already has the right taxonomy, missing, revoked, expired, missed_sunday, expiring (app/jobs/schwab/token_health_job.rb:17-24), but it is private to the job. Extract it to `SchwabToken.status` and use it in the banner, the system page, the mailer, and `get_account_health` in step 8. That is the single method step 7 most needs and does not have.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:17:**5. Which account is the dashboard about?** Every query in the design says "the latest balance" and "positions," but the IRA syncs too, hourly, with balances and positions. Equity, open risk, cash, and the positions list must be scoped to `Account.trading`. The IRA gets one collapsed line with equity and its as-of stamp, or nothing in Phase 1. With zero trading accounts, which is the state on first login, the dashboard body is the setup card, not an empty positions list.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:21:**7. Distance to stop is nil exactly when it matters most.** `Position#distance_to_stop` returns nil unless `protected?` (app/models/position.rb:36-39). A partially covered or oversized stop has a price, and its distance is the actionable number; the coverage problem is the inline warning. Guard on `stop_price.present?` instead and keep `open_risk` as it is. Sort order for the list: unprotected, awaiting, and trailing-unknown first, then ascending distance, so a negative distance, price already through the stop, is the loudest row. The wireframe promises a distance bar; a bar needs a scale. Use the entry-to-stop distance as 100 percent and cap the fill, or drop the bar for Phase 1 and show the number.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:23:**8. Staleness has no shared cadence.** "Older than its cadence" means the interval `Sync::TickJob` would pick right now for that account and feed: 15 or 5 minutes in session for a trading account, 60 otherwise, and 60 always for read-only accounts. Those constants live inside the job (app/jobs/sync/tick_job.rb:4-5). Extract `Account#sync_interval(feed)` so the tick and the view cannot disagree, and define stale as older than twice that interval plus the minute of slack, or any age when `sync_paused_reason` is set. The distance-to-stop number depends on two feeds: `last_price` from positions and `stop_price` from orders. Orders have no `synced_at`, and `updated_at` does not move when an upsert changes nothing, so the stop's as-of is the `finished_at` of the latest advanced-cursor orders `SyncRun` for the account. Show the older of the two stamps on that number. A failed run with a usable token has no banner state; the stale mark plus a one-line "last positions sync failed: error" under the header covers it.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:25:**9. Two conditions at once hide the only call to action.** Precedence halted > expired means a manual halt buries the re-auth button while sync is dead. In Phase 1 the halt does nothing but paint a banner. Keep the precedence if you want, but the banner area must carry a secondary status line for any other active condition, and the re-auth link must survive under halted. The halted copy is also wrong as wireframed: Phase 1 has no tripped rule and no reset time. It reads "Halted by John, Mon 11:14a: reason. Clear it on the System page." Do not render the disabled "New proposal" button; there is no such entry point.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:27:**10. The expiring rule will make Playwright flaky if it follows the mailer.** The mailer suppresses the 24-hour warning when Sunday's email covers it. If the banner does the same, whether it shows depends on the wall-clock weekday when the test runs. Use the plain `refresh_expiring_soon?` for the banner and add "Sunday's email will remind you" to the copy when covered. Deterministic, and honest.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:31:**12. The account-setup path is missing pieces.** Needs-setup means `account_type` nil, not `trading_enabled` false; a classified IRA is done. Three things to add: a validation that `trading_enabled` requires `taxable` (the PRD says trading other accounts is a non-goal); an `account_configured` audit kind, since this decides what gets journaled; and an immediate enqueue of positions, orders, and activities for that account on enable, because the tick otherwise waits up to an hour off-hours and `Journal::LinkFillsJob` only runs after an activities sync. The operator also has to tell two hashes apart. Show each account's latest equity and top symbols on the setup card; `Sync::CatchUpJob` has already synced both accounts read-only by then. Let the operator set `nickname` in the same form. The dashboard callout links to the system page's accounts section.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:35:## Per-screen checks and the Playwright plan
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:37:**Dashboard content vs Flow 1.** Equity, settled and unsettled cash, open risk with the excluded count, positions with distance first and P&L second: all producible once items 2, 5, 6, 7, and 8 land. Unrealized P&L is `market_value` minus `cost_basis`, both present when `average_price` is. `settled_cash` can be nil when both readings are nil (app/models/schwab/balances.rb:20-22); render "unavailable," never zero. The pending proposals row has nothing to link to; render "Proposals: Phase 2" without a link, or omit it. Two other empty states exist beyond pre-first-sync: a trading account with zero positions, all cash, says "No open positions," and token-present-but-no-sync-yet says "Waiting for the first sync" with the sync runs' status. The current dashboard view has the connect copy but no button (app/views/dashboard/show.html.erb:4).
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:39:**System page vs Flow 8 and §5.10.** Fillable now: token age and status, `refresh_expires_at`, next Sunday 18:00 marked with a loud line when the token dies before it, last success and latest status per feed per account from `SyncRun`, `gap_from` when set, pause reason, failed `SyncRun` count plus `SolidQueue::FailedExecution` in 7 days with truncated errors, shadow mode as a read-only indicator, accounts table with the inline form. Honest "not yet" rows: API spend shows "0 runs, briefs start in step 9," and the memory repo feed shows "never." No shadow-mode toggle in Phase 1; nothing to shadow. For the kill switch, use one word everywhere: the flows doc says "Pause system," the audit kinds say `manual_halt_*`, and "paused" already means sync. Call it Halt. Flow 8 puts the typed confirmation on unhalt; that is a required text field checked server-side, not a Stimulus confirm, which removes the only JS in the step. Set requires a reason and audits `manual_halt_set` with `Current.user`; clear audits `manual_halt_cleared`. "Halted by" comes from the latest `manual_halt_set` audit event; no new column.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:41:**Trade screens vs Flow 4.** Post-mortem: two inputs, one line plus followed or improvised, on any closed trade. `post_mortem` normalizes blank to nil (app/models/trade.rb:18), so a followed flag with empty text leaves the trade in `missing_post_mortem`; require the text. When a closed trade also needs review, the review form renders first. Planned versus actual stop: for open trades the actual is the position's working stop looked up by account and instrument; for closed stopped-out trades it is the closing exit price. Trade index needs a `missing_post_mortem` filter, since the EOD email deep-links there. `journal_completed_at` is set by review, not by the post-mortem; decide what it means or stop writing it.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:43:**Playwright.** Draw the scenarios route only inside `if Rails.env.test?` in routes, and guard again in the controller with `Rails.env.test? && Schwab.fake?`; development uses the fake adapter too and must not be resettable by a GET. The route must sign in a seeded user and set the session cookie, because the test mail adapter gives Playwright no inbox to read the magic link from. Call `Schwab::FakeClient.instance.reset!` on every scenario. Set the queue adapter explicitly for the Playwright server; test.rb does not set one, so `SchwabToken.issue!` enqueuing `Sync::CatchUpJob` would run on the async adapter in the background. Seed rows directly with the factories, not by driving jobs. Make times relative and unambiguous under either cadence: fresh is `Time.current`, stale is three hours ago, expiring is 22 hours out, expired is two days ago. Scenarios beyond the four banners: not connected, needs setup, one unprotected position (the fixture has none, both XYZ and DEF are protected), a failed sync with a usable token, the review queue with Skip persisting across reload, and the post-mortem save. Re-auth success needs the seeded account hash to match `Schwab::FakeClient::ACCOUNT_HASH` or `verify_accounts!` rejects it (app/models/schwab_token/reauth.rb:22-27).
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:45:**Hotwire Native.** Every screen a full page with its own URL and a short `content_for :title`, since the native nav bar uses it. No slide-over detail panel in Phase 1. No `data-turbo-confirm` or `window.confirm`; typed confirmation is server-side. Positions as a list of rows, not a table. Redirect after every POST. The OAuth redirect uses `allow_other_host`, which the native shell will need to open externally in Phase 2; note it in the path configuration, nothing to change now. `allow_browser versions: :modern` checks the user agent; the Hotwire Native user agent passes as Safari today, but keep it in mind when the shell ships. Refresh on load only; Turbo Streams for sync completions are Phase 2.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:53:| `SchwabToken.status` extracted from the health job | `SchwabToken`, `TokenHealthJob` | Item 3; one taxonomy for banner, system page, mailer, MCP |
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:57:| `trading_enabled` requires `taxable`; `account_configured` audit kind; enqueue sync on enable | `Account`, `AuditEvent::KINDS`, system controller | Item 12 |
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:3:1. **The halted dashboard banner is over-designed for Phase 1.**  
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:4:   Flow 1’s halted state is a rule-driven halt: rule name, trip time, reset time, exits allowed. Phase 1 only has `SystemSettings.manual_halt`, `manual_halt_reason`, and `manual_halt_at`. It cannot honestly render “daily loss tripped” or “resumes tomorrow.”  
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:5:   Action: Phase 1 banner copy must say “Paused manually” with reason/time. Defer rule-halt copy until a halt model or fields like `halt_source`, `halt_rule`, `halt_resets_at` exist.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:8:   `halted > expired > expiring > healthy` is not enough. The screen must distinguish:
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:17:3. **System health wants API spend before Phase 1 produces it.**  
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:21:4. **The dashboard day-change number needs a real read model/query.**  
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:23:   Action: add a dashboard query object that returns current equity, prior snapshot, net flows since prior snapshot, day change amount, day change percent, and “no prior snapshot” state.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:25:5. **Risk-budget UI from the Monarch note cannot ship in Phase 1.**  
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:26:   Guardrail headroom bars need active `risk_rules`, max risk per trade, daily loss limit, sector exposure, and max positions. Phase 1 explicitly has no guardrail engine and empty `risk_rules`.  
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:32:   Phase 1 can produce symbol, quantity, cost basis, market value, last price, `protection`, `distance_to_stop`, `open_risk`, and `synced_at`. Missing or unstated:
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:40:   The model intentionally sums protected positions only. That is correct, but the dashboard must not imply unprotected positions are zero risk.  
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:45:   - balances/positions for trading accounts: stale after 15 min during session, 60 min off-hours
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:46:   - orders/activities: stale after 5 min during session, 60 min off-hours
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:51:   If sync is paused, mark broker-derived values stale regardless of age.  
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:66:12. **“Not a trade” should preserve the journal object.**  
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:72:13. Phase 1 can fill token age, next Sunday cadence, last sync per feed, sync pause reason, failed `SyncRun`/`AgentRun`, Solid Queue failures, shadow mode, and manual halt state.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:74:14. Phase 1 cannot honestly fill API spend until step 9 agent runs exist.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:76:15. The halt toggle must require a reason on pause and typed confirmation on unpause. Audit both with user, reason, previous reason, and timestamp.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:78:16. Account setup must be a blocking operator path. New accounts arrive with `account_type = nil` and `trading_enabled = false`; nothing journals until the operator classifies the taxable account and enables it. Add an audit event for this change.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:80:**Playwright**
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:87:   - expired: expired token, paused reason/time, stale balance/positions
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:88:   - halted: healthy token plus `manual_halt`, reason, timestamp
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:94:20. Avoid hover-only slideovers and modal-only flows. Trade review and system halt confirmation must be normal server-rendered routes on mobile.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:96:21. Do not make Stimulus `confirm()` the only safety mechanism for the halt toggle. A typed confirmation form will survive the future native wrapper better.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:98:Bottom line: Step 7 should build the screens, but with honest Phase 1 data boundaries. The biggest correction is to stop rendering future guardrail/proposal/halt concepts as if the data already exists.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:7:Before build step 7 (the Phase 1 web screens: dashboard with four banner states, system health, trade review and post-mortem, plus Playwright) is written, review the screen design against the PRD and the UI flows doc, and find what the screens need from the data model that Phase 1 does not produce.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:12:- @docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md §5.8 (UI), §5.8a (iOS later: keep screens mobile-responsive, no full-page JS routers, no hover-dependent modals), §5.9 (shadow mode indicator), §5.10 (health page shows token age and Sunday cadence)
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:13:- @docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md Flow 1 (dashboard states and content), Flow 4 (journal entry), Flow 8 (system health and kill switch), cross-cutting states (stale data marks, token expired read-only mode, empty states), the Monarch and Midday/Mercury/Origin reference notes (distance-to-stop as the primary number, unprotected inline warning, freshness stamps, orphan review modal with N-more-to-review, sparkle glyph on agent-authored content)
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:14:- @docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-wireframes.html (Flow 1 frames, Flow 4 frame, Flow 8 frame)
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:15:- @docs/phase-1-plan.md §7 (screens table, app mark, banner precedence), §8 (Playwright scenarios), §5 (protection states)
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:18:Models and jobs from steps 2 through 6: Account (trading_enabled, account_type nullable), Position (#protection returning :protected/:partial/:oversized/:awaiting/:trailing_unknown/:unprotected, #distance_to_stop, #open_risk, synced_at), Balance (equity, settled_cash, unsettled_cash, as_of), Order, Activity, Trade (status, needs_review, review_reason enum, bootstrapped, excluded_from_stats, stopped_out, planned_stop, avg_entry/avg_exit, realized_pnl, realized_r, post_mortem, followed_setup, review!, exclude!), Setup (stats), Snapshot (equity, daily_return, index_value, high_water_index, drawdown, open_risk_amount, open_risk_ratio, unprotected_count), SchwabToken (usable?, refresh_expiring_soon?, revoked?, age via issued_at), SystemSettings (shadow_mode, manual_halt, manual_halt_reason, sync_paused_reason), SyncRun (per feed and account, status, started_at, finished_at, error), AgentRun (estimated_cost; table exists, populated in step 9), MarketDay, AuditEvent. Magic-link login with two users. Layout shell with the Athayde crest. Schwab::FakeClient with a scripted queue and a fake authorize page; a test-only scenario route is planned for Playwright.
