agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:3:# Step 6 design review: journal builder, setup stats, snapshots
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:5:## Critical: will produce wrong journal rows on day one
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:11:**2. Forward splits, stock dividends, and ACAT deliveries are classified as `transfer` and the design drops them.** The mapper returns `corporate_action` only when an activity carries two security items and `transfer` when it carries one (app/models/schwab/activity.rb:52). A 2:1 split on the same CUSIP arrives as one RECEIVE_AND_DELIVER with a single item for the 40 new shares. The design lists only cash-only transfers, so a transfer with an instrument and an open trade is silently stamped journaled with no leg. Trade quantity stays at 40, the broker says 80, and selling 80 drives running quantity to negative 40. The ratio is not on the activity. It has to be derived: (running quantity + delivered quantity) / running quantity, or reconciled against the broker position.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:14:- **Return of capital is unreachable.** A ROC arrives as DIVIDEND_OR_INTEREST with a security, which maps to `dividend`, so it will always become an income leg. Drop the basis-adjustment path for Phase 1 and treat it as income. Realized P&L is identical either way. Only basis attribution differs.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:16:- **No trade-without-position reconciliation.** Bootstrap only covers positions without a trade. If A's succession activity never arrives, or a position is delivered out by ACAT, A's trade stays open with no position indefinitely. After each complete positions sync, any open trade whose instrument has no position and no unjournaled fills should be flagged needing review with a reason.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:26:- On the scale-in question: keep R denominated in initial risk. That is the standard definition and it is what expectancy per setup means. Store total risk, the sum of each entry leg's quantity times its distance to the stop at that time, as a second column for the journal browser, but do not divide by it.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:40:**6. Recompute trades from legs, never incrementally.** If the job crashes after inserting a leg and before updating the trade and stamping `journaled_at`, the rerun hits the unique leg index and the trade aggregates are stale. Wrap leg insert, trade recompute, and `journaled_at` in one transaction per activity, and make trade fields a pure function of the legs in `executed_at` order.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:44:**8. Re-synced activities are not handled.** The upsert overwrites price, quantity, and status. A VALID to INVALID flip after journaling leaves a leg for a busted trade. A corrected price leaves a stale leg. Clear `journaled_at` and drop the leg when a journaled activity's quantity, price, or status changes on upsert. ACTIVITY_CORRECTION rows need a decision too.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:70:## What the EOD brief and dashboard need that is not produced
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:72:- **Day change** on the dashboard should be flow-adjusted: equity minus flows minus prior snapshot equity. Derivable, but only if the prior snapshot exists. Say what to show on a gap day.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:73:- **Trailing-20 trend** per setup for the Sunday edge review is not in the stats columns. Either add it or defer it visibly.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:74:- **Stopped-out flag.** Flow 4 shows planned versus actual stop. Whether the exit came from the stop child order is derivable through the exit leg's activity and its order type, but nothing records it. Add it at close time.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:75:- **Fills recap** for the EOD should read activities journaled today, not trades created today. Both are needed and neither is named as a query.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:7:Sequence: legacy holding is 40 shares. First synced journalable fill is `sell 15`.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:24:If the system bootstraps 15, it immediately closes the trade and treats the remaining 25 as a separate new bootstrapped trade on the next positions sync. That splits one lifecycle into two fake trades and corrupts setup stats, P&L, and missing-review UX.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:28:2. **`journaled_at` is not a safe idempotency boundary.**
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:30:The design says unique `trade_legs.activity_id` gives idempotency and every processed activity gets `journaled_at`. That is insufficient because one activity can drive multiple durable side effects: create trade, create leg, mutate trade aggregates, mutate instrument succession, journal activity.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:36:| leg inserted, trade aggregates not recomputed | activity may be skipped if `journaled_at` was set early, leaving stale trade totals |
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:41:Fix: process each activity in one DB transaction with row locks on account/instrument/open trade. Insert/find the leg by `activity_id`, then recompute the affected trade from all legs, then set `journaled_at` last. Reruns should be “find existing leg and recompute,” not “skip because activity is marked.”
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:90:A bootstrapped trade can close before the user reviews it. If the user later enters setup and planned stop, the system can compute a number, but it is not the same quality as a planned trade captured at entry.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:101:Otherwise the Sunday edge review will mix real strategy executions with reconstructed history.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:128:A reverse merger replacing CUSIP A with CUSIP B in one activity needs multiple journal effects: remove/convert old shares, add new shares, possibly cash-in-lieu, ratio, and instrument succession. But `trade_legs.activity_id` is unique. That allows only one leg per Schwab activity.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:219:| broker position absent but trade open | close only if a journaled exit/corporate action proves zero; otherwise flag |
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:222:Add `computed_quantity` either as a stored field or a deterministic query, and compare it to `positions.quantity` after each sync. Raise dashboard/system-health review items for mismatches.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:226:The plan says journal builder runs trading-enabled accounts only, which is correct. But the design review must explicitly preserve this:
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:231:| taxable trade in same instrument | taxable journal unaffected |
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:232:| IRA buy after taxable loss | future wash-sale warning/block context, not Phase 1 journal mutation |
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:281:Using “latest on or before” across missing days can smear a stale equity value over market days and fake zero returns.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:291:EOD requires “journal rows created” and “rows missing post-mortems.” Dashboard requires review counts, drawdown, open risk, stale data, and unprotected count.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:300:| dashboard risk | snapshot `open_risk_amount` sums only protected positions; must surface excluded unknown risk count |
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:302:| audit trail | review path audits, but auto journal corrections should also produce system audit or at least sync diagnostic events |
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:306:Build step 6 around a deterministic journal ledger, not direct mutation from each activity.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:311:2. Process account+instrument journal changes under an advisory lock or row lock.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:313:4. Set `journaled_at` only after all side effects commit.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:319:The most important correction before implementation: do not let sell-first bootstrap, first-entry-only R, and date-only ordering ship as designed. Those three will produce wrong journal data immediately on a real account.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:7:Before build step 6 (the trade journal builder, setup stats, and daily snapshots) is written, review the design against the PRD and find where it will produce wrong journal data or wrong drawdown numbers on a real account.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:12:- @docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md §5.2 (`trades`: one instrument's position lifecycle from zero back to zero; scale-ins and scale-outs as `trade_legs`; orphan fills create a trade in incomplete state with no planned stop; `setups` rolling stats; `snapshots` flow-adjusted equity), §5.3 (corporate actions and dividends adjust journal cost basis automatically), §5.7 (EOD lists rows missing post-mortems), §5.11 item 5 (fixture payloads including corporate-action and dividend events, verifying journal linking)
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:13:- @docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md Flow 4 (post-trade journal entry) and the Monarch "orphan fill review" addendum
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:14:- @docs/phase-1-plan.md §4 (journal builder rules: bootstrap, link fills, leg kinds, R math, CUSIP succession, review path), §6 (snapshots: chain-linked index, per account, rebuildable, flows), §1 rows for trades, trade_legs, setups, snapshots
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:17:- Models: Trade (status open/closed, needs_review, bootstrapped, opened_at nullable, avg_entry/avg_exit, peak_quantity, planned_stop/target, initial_risk, realized_pnl, realized_r, thesis, post_mortem, followed_setup, journal_completed_at; partial unique index: one open trade per account and instrument), TradeLeg (kind entry/exit/adjustment/income with prefix, quantity, price, ratio, cash_amount, executed_at nullable, activity_id unique where present), Activity (kind fill/sweep/dividend/interest/fee/deposit/withdrawal/transfer/corporate_action/other, status, side, quantity, price, commission, fees, net_amount, trade_date, executed_at, journaled_at, order_id → orders.order_proposal_id), Setup (stats columns), Snapshot (account, as_of unique, equity, net_flows, daily_return, index_value default 1, high_water_index default 1, drawdown fraction, open_risk_amount, open_risk_ratio, unprotected_count), Balance (time series per account), Position (#protection, #open_risk), Instrument (predecessor_instrument_id, rename!).
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:18:- Step 5 sync: activities arrive with kinds and `valid_for_journal` scope; positions carry average_price from the broker; Sync::PositionsJob and Sync::ActivitiesJob will enqueue Journal::BootstrapJob and Journal::LinkFillsJob.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:23:- `Journal::LinkFillsJob(account)`: unjournaled VALID activities in `executed_at` order, per instrument: buy fill with no open trade opens one (copying setup/thesis/planned stop from the originating proposal when `order.order_proposal_id` resolves, else `needs_review`); sell fill with no open trade bootstraps first (quantity from the fill) then applies the exit; every fill is an entry or exit leg with running quantity, avg_entry, avg_exit, peak_quantity recomputed from legs; quantity reaching zero closes the trade with realized_pnl = exits − entries − commissions − fees + income legs; `initial_risk` = first entry quantity × (entry price − planned_stop) fixed when the stop is known; realized_r = realized_pnl / initial_risk or nil. Dividend/interest with a matching open trade: income leg (feeds realized_pnl, not basis). Splits: adjustment leg with ratio, scaling quantity, avg_entry, planned_stop, planned_target. Return of capital: adjustment leg with cash_amount adjusting avg_entry. CUSIP succession (corporate_action with two securities): set predecessor_instrument_id on the new instrument and move the open trade to it with an adjustment leg; unmatched halves fall back to exit/entry with needs_review. Symbol change on a known CUSIP: rename only. Idempotent via the unique activity_id on legs; every processed activity gets journaled_at.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:24:- Sweeps, deposits, withdrawals, transfers, fees without an instrument: journaled_at set, no leg.
agents/counselors/1788302368-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:37:- Check what the EOD brief and the dashboard need from these tables that the design does not produce
