agents/counselors/1788307777-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:17:- Models: Position (#protection, #distance_to_stop, #open_risk, #unrealized_pnl, synced_at), Balance, Account (trading, label, sync_interval, last_sync), Trade (status, needs_review, review_reason, realized_r, legs), Setup (stats), Snapshot (drawdown, index), SchwabToken.status, SystemSettings (shadow_mode, manual_halt, sync_paused_reason), SyncRun, ToolCall (agent_run_id nullable, transport mcp|scheduled, tool_name, arguments jsonb, duration_ms, error), Dashboard read model (banner, rows, open_risk, excluded_by_reason, day_change, staleness), Schwab::Client (quotes returning pages, price_history) with Schwab.client(wait: false) for web callers and Schwab::Quote.batch / Schwab::PriceHistory mappers, Rails.cache (Solid Cache in production).
agents/counselors/1788307777-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:23:- Tools return plain hashes (JSON-serializable) with every number carrying its as-of time and a `stale` flag from the same staleness rule the dashboard uses; account hashes never appear; symbols appear alongside CUSIP.
agents/counselors/1788307777-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:24:- `POST /mcp` via the `mcp` gem's Streamable HTTP transport mounted in Rails (a controller action delegating to `MCP::Server#handle_json`), bearer compared with secure_compare, 401 rendering a plain "MCP auth failed" page (Playwright target), CSRF skipped for that route, JSON only.
