agents/counselors/1788307777-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:27:- get_account_health returns token status and age, sync status per feed, pause reason, shadow mode, halt, equity, settled/unsettled cash, drawdown from the latest snapshot, unprotected count and reasons.
agents/counselors/1788307777-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:34:- Check each tool's input schema and output for what the agent actually needs (PRD §5.7 briefs): symbols versus CUSIP, date ranges, pagination or limits on get_journal, what get_portfolio includes for unprotected positions, how staleness is represented
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:3:# Step 6 build review: journal builder, setup stats, snapshots
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:7:**1. The split and transfer path is dead in production; the spec fabricates the input.** The mapper only sets `quantity` for TRADE activities at `app/models/schwab/activity.rb:36`. A RECEIVE_AND_DELIVER with one security item lands in the activities table with `quantity: nil`, so `link_transfer` returns at `app/models/journal/linker.rb:76` and the activity is stamped journaled with no leg. The 2:1 split spec builds the row by hand with `quantity: 40`, which the sync will never produce. The same nil zeroes out share transfers in `Snapshot.net_flows` at `app/models/snapshot.rb:43`. Direction is also wrong: `linker.rb:80` derives it from the sign of `net_amount`, which is zero on any share delivery, so an outbound ACAT or a reverse-split share removal reads as inbound. Fix: read the signed security amount from `Schwab::Activity.from(activity.raw).securities.first` the way `link_corporate_action` already does, or have the mapper populate quantity and a signed direction for non-TRADE security items. Add a spec that goes through the mapper.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:12:- `Journal::LinkFillsJob` at `app/jobs/journal/link_fills_job.rb:8-9` reconciles against whatever positions row exists. Activities sync every 5 minutes, positions every 15. A partial sell linked before the next positions sync sees the stale higher quantity and creates a plug. The plug is deleted 10 minutes later, but `bootstrapped: true`, `needs_review: true`, and `review_reason: bootstrapped` stay.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:13:- `Journal::BootstrapJob` at `app/jobs/journal/bootstrap_job.rb:11-12` does the mirror image on every scale-in whose buy has not synced yet.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:14:- `bootstrap_job.rb:16-19` flags `position_missing` on every normal full exit when the positions sync runs before the activities sync, because the sell is not yet an unjournaled activity. That reason outranks everything but corporate_action and ordering, and nothing clears it when the exit links and closes the trade.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:19:**4. One exception stops journaling for the whole account permanently.** `link_all!` at `linker.rb:9` iterates chronologically with no per-activity rescue, so a failing activity aborts the loop, the job fails, and every later activity stays unjournaled on every rerun. Concrete triggers already in the code:
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:34:**8. `planned_stop` is mutated per link, so a re-sync of a split or succession corrupts it.** `linker.rb:84` and `linker.rb:113` divide the stop on create. `Activity#unjournal!` drops the leg, and the relink divides it again. For a succession the relink cannot even find the old trade because it already moved, so `flag_orphans` runs and the adjustment leg is never recreated. Fix: keep the stop in original-entry units and derive the displayed stop through the cumulative ratio. `compute_initial_risk` already multiplies the stop back by the factor, so the code is fighting itself.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:36:**9. An oversold trade with no position never reconciles.** Both journal jobs iterate positions only. A plug built from a stale 40 followed by a sell of 60 leaves running −20 and no closing leg, the position row is deleted, and the trade sits open at −20 with `position_missing`. Reconciling open trades without a position against broker quantity 0 is safe: a negative plug is a no-op, so only the missing-entry case gets fixed.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:42:**12. `unjournal!` at `app/models/activity.rb:29-34` is not transactional.** A crash between `destroy!` and `update!` loses the activity from the journal for good. It also runs under the activities concurrency key, not the journal key, so it can race a running `LinkFillsJob`.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:46:**14. Succession details.** Ratio at `linker.rb:108-110` uses `trade.quantity` rather than the out security's amount, so any journal drift changes the ratio. The `position_missing` suppression at `bootstrap_job.rb:18` keys on `activity.instrument_id`, which is whichever security came first in the payload. The fallback when one side is missing only flags; the plan said exit/entry legs.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:48:**15. Setup stats staleness.** `review!` at `trade.rb:96` recomputes only the new setup. A trade moved from setup A to B leaves A's stored stats counting it until A happens to have another closed trade in the blanket recompute at `link_fills_job.rb:11`.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:62:| Reverse merger A to B, bootstrapped B | trade moved, ratio 0.5, avg 100 | matches; reviewed B raises and halts the account (item 4) |
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:66:`recompute!` itself is correct for ratio adjustments, income legs, and the plug sorting first. Precision, peak, average entry after a split, and the closing rule all trace clean. The per-activity transaction and `journaled_at` last are right. The shared concurrency key with `on_conflict: :discard` drops the second job rather than queuing it, which is acceptable since both are idempotent and rerun on the next sync, but note it means a bootstrap after a positions sync can be skipped for up to 15 minutes.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:68:**Missing specs**, each of which would have caught a finding above: transfer and succession rows built through `Schwab::Activity.from` and the activities upsert; BootstrapJob after a split; LinkFillsJob against a stale positions row after a partial sell; BootstrapJob before the buy syncs; `review!` then BootstrapJob on an open legacy holding; full exit with positions ahead of activities; sell-before-buy with equal timestamps; legacy sell with no position; `unjournal!` on a split activity then relink; a plug-plus-scale-in trade reviewed and checked against `eligible_for_stats`; an exception on one activity leaving later ones linked; RebuildJob at 10:00 followed by the tick at 16:25; first-snapshot `net_flows`; a withdrawal with a positive `net_amount`; two RebuildJobs concurrently. The `rescue` at `spec/jobs/journal/hooks_spec.rb:31` should be replaced with a snapshot factory.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/prompt.md:7:Is `docs/phase-1-plan.md` a faithful, complete, and well-designed reading of Phase 1 of the Investment Copilot PRD? Find gaps, contradictions, and design decisions that will have to be undone in Phase 2. The PRD is the source of truth; where the kickoff brief and the PRD disagree, the PRD wins.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/prompt.md:14:- @docs/artifacts/claude-code-kickoff.md (Phase 1 scope brief and constraints)
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/prompt.md:15:- @docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md (screen states; Phase 1 needs dashboard banners, re-auth, health, journal quick entry)
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/prompt.md:20:### Phase 1 scope reminder
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/prompt.md:21:Read-only: Schwab OAuth + token lifecycle, sync (accounts, positions, balances, orders, transactions, market hours), journal auto-population from fills using the zero-to-zero trade definition keyed by CUSIP, dashboard with four banner states, MCP read tools over HTTPS with bearer auth, scheduled Anthropic Messages API runs (07:00 brief, 16:30 EOD, Sunday stub) with read-only tools and a hard tool-turn cap, shadow-mode flag, memory-repo pull. Migrations for every §5.2 table even where Phase 1 does not populate them. Not in Phase 1: guardrails, proposals, approval UI, submission, brackets, allocation module, FMP.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/prompt.md:27:- Check the token lifecycle design against §5.1 and §5.10 (25-minute refresh, 7-day hard expiry, degrade-and-queue rather than skip, Sunday ritual and Mon/Tue escalation)
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/prompt.md:28:- Check the journal builder rules against §5.2 `trades`/`trade_legs` and the corporate-action, dividend, scale-in/out, orphan-fill, and ticker-change cases
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/prompt.md:33:- Flag anything the plan builds that the PRD explicitly defers, and anything the PRD requires in Phase 1 that the plan omits
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/claude-fable.md:1:**Verdict:** the plan is a faithful reading of Phase 1 scope and its table list covers every §5.2 table. It is not yet complete or Phase 2 safe. Six problems will force schema or model rewrites, and two of them will produce wrong journal data on day one with the real account.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/claude-fable.md:5:**1. CUSIP is not a stable key across corporate actions, and the plan treats it as one.** Reverse splits, mergers, and spinoffs issue a new CUSIP. The PRD says CUSIP so ticker changes cannot break linking, which is true, but the plan's journal rule only handles "symbol changes on a known CUSIP". A CUSIP change arrives as an out on the old instrument and an in on a new one. The zero-to-zero builder will close the old trade with a phantom exit and open a new incomplete trade with no history. Add `predecessor_instrument_id` to instruments now and a builder rule that carries the open trade across a succession event. Also drop `not null` on cusip or add a fallback natural key. Schwab positions and transaction items for cash equivalents, sweeps, and possibly options may arrive without a CUSIP. Store Schwab's integer `instrumentId` alongside. Mark all of this as shape unverified.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/claude-fable.md:11:**4. The flow-adjusted equity math is wrong for the account it serves.** Subtracting cumulative net flows produces an additive series. On a small account that receives meaningful deposits, the adjusted series stays near the starting balance while daily dollar moves scale with the real balance, so drawdown percent explodes. A 1 percent move on a book that grew tenfold through deposits reads as a 10 percent drawdown. Phase 2's drawdown halt will trip on that number. Use a chain-linked daily return index, with each day's return computed net of that day's flows, and compute HWM and drawdown on the index. Two more problems in the same table: `snapshots` has no account_id, so IRA equity pollutes the trading account's drawdown, and there is no recompute path when a deposit's transaction record lands a day after the balance moved. Make snapshots per account and rebuildable from balances plus transactions.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/claude-fable.md:17:## Significant: Phase 2 will undo it, or Phase 1 behaves wrong
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/claude-fable.md:24:- **IRA fills will create journal trades.** The builder runs "for each account and instrument". Restrict it to accounts with `trading_enabled`. IRA transactions still sync for Phase 2 wash-sale checks.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/claude-fable.md:25:- **Positions are upserted, never removed.** A closed position stays on the dashboard forever. Delete or zero rows absent from the broker response.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/claude-fable.md:26:- **Token gating will spawn a job storm.** The tick job enqueues every 5 minutes, and every gated job re-enqueues itself 15 minutes later, so the queue grows without bound during a multi-day expiry. Replace re-enqueue with a paused state and a single catch-up sync enqueued from the re-auth callback, with the transactions window widened to cover the gap. Decide explicitly whether brief jobs run degraded with stale data or wait. Running them with an "as of" disclaimer is more useful and still satisfies §5.1.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/claude-fable.md:27:- **State that the 7-day clock never resets on access refresh.** The schema separates `issued_at` from `last_refreshed_at`, which is right, but one community source found in my search claims refreshes roll the window forward. That is wrong per Schwab's own docs. Write the rule into the plan so nobody "fixes" it later. Also define the Mon and Tue escalation condition precisely: escalate when `refresh_expires_at` falls before the next Sunday email plus a buffer.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/claude-fable.md:30:- **Two seeded users contradicts §3 and §7.** The PRD says single user, John only. If a second login stays, `audit_events` needs a `user_id` now, because Phase 2 approvals must be attributable to a person.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/claude-fable.md:41:- Magic-link login depends on Resend, and re-auth depends on login. An email outage locks John out of the one action that keeps the system alive. Add a console-generated login link as a fallback.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/claude-fable.md:47:**What the plan gets right and should keep:** one tool registry with two transports, market calendar as the only source of "market hours", the append-only trigger on audits, `sync_runs` per feed, the fake client boundary for Playwright and seeds, the shape-unverified marker convention, and the decision to omit `evaluate_hypothetical_order` until the guardrail engine exists.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:3:1. [app/models/schwab/activity.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/schwab/activity.rb:36) leaves `quantity` nil for non-TRADE activities, so real split/ACAT transfer rows will be stamped journaled with no leg.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:4:`Journal::Linker#link_transfer` requires `activity.quantity` ([linker.rb:76](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/journal/linker.rb:76)), but the mapper only sets quantity for trades. The split spec bypasses the mapper by hand-building an activity with quantity, so it proves the wrong path. Result: 2:1 split still produces wrong journal quantity and later sells can drive the trade negative.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:10:Activities sort by `executed_at, id` ([activity.rb:15](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/activity.rb:15)), and ambiguity is flagged only when a new leg is strictly earlier than the latest existing leg ([linker.rb:38](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/journal/linker.rb:38)). Equal date-only timestamps are not flagged. A sell row ingested before a same-day buy still creates a fake bootstrapped closed trade, then the buy opens a second trade.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:12:4. Sell exceeding the current journal quantity is not handled.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:13:`Trade#recompute!` allows running quantity to go negative and leaves the trade open with nonsense aggregates ([trade.rb:64](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/trade.rb:64), [trade.rb:77](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/trade.rb:77)). This will happen on missing exits/transfers, stale positions, or bad ordering. It should split/flag/quarantine, not produce an open trade with negative quantity.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:30:`link_fill` returns on nil instrument/side/quantity ([linker.rb:29](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/journal/linker.rb:29)), but `link!` still stamps `journaled_at` ([linker.rb:21](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/journal/linker.rb:21)). That silently loses fills instead of quarantining them.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:33:If one side of succession is missing, `flag_orphans` only flags open trades it can resolve ([linker.rb:119](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/journal/linker.rb:119)), then the activity is stamped journaled. It does not create fallback exit/entry rows, preserve the unresolved payload for review, or prevent one-sided corporate actions from disappearing.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:35:11. `stopped_out` can become stale.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:36:It is set after a stop exit closes a trade ([linker.rb:41](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/journal/linker.rb:41)), but `recompute!` never recalculates or clears it. If the stop fill is corrected/invalidated and `unjournal!` removes the leg, the trade can remain marked stopped out.
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:40:The plug-leg design is mostly present: `reconcile_plug!` exists, plug legs sort first, the link job has a second reconcile pass, and bootstrap/link share the `"journal-#{account.id}"` concurrency key. P&L from leg `cash_amount` is also the right direction, and setup stats now exclude `needs_review`, `excluded_from_stats`, and non-positive risk.
agents/counselors/1788301084-review-request-question-review-build-st/prompt.md:7:Review build step 4 of Phase 1: the Schwab OAuth round trip and token lifecycle, built to the design you reviewed earlier (your findings on the Monday/Tuesday escalation rule, stale-row pauses, callback idempotency, and account binding were all incorporated). Verify the fixes actually hold, and find what is still wrong.
agents/counselors/1788301084-review-request-question-review-build-st/prompt.md:29:- Re-derive the Monday/Tuesday rule from the code and check it against: re-auth Sunday 18:30 then Monday 08:00 (no nag), re-auth Wednesday then next Monday (nag), token issued Sunday 17:00 before the email (edge case), DST transitions
agents/counselors/1788301084-review-request-question-review-build-st/prompt.md:30:- Trace refresh! for: two processes hitting 401 at once; a refresh in flight when issue! inserts a new row; a ReauthRequired on a stale row; a ServerError; a response missing refresh_token; whether the rescue outside with_lock can observe rolled-back state; whether the debounce can suppress a needed refresh after a failed one
agents/counselors/1788305713-review-request-question-review-build-st/prompt.md:7:Review build step 6 of Phase 1: the trade journal builder, setup stats, and daily snapshots, built to the design you reviewed (plug-leg bootstrap reconciled to the broker, transactional per-activity linking with full recompute from legs, leg cash amounts for P&L, initial quantity from the first order, flows since the prior snapshot, type-first withdrawal classification). Verify the fixes hold in the code and find what will still produce wrong journal rows or drawdown numbers.
