agents/counselors/1788300021-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:19:- Step 2: `schwab_tokens` table (access_token and refresh_token encrypted, access_expires_at, refresh_expires_at NOT NULL and never moved by a refresh, issued_at, last_refreshed_at, last_refresh_error, scope), `audit_events` with `AuditEvent::KINDS` including re_auth_succeeded, re_auth_failed, token_refresh_failed, sync_paused_token_expired, sync_resumed, token_nag_sent; `system_settings.sync_paused_reason`; `sync_runs`.
agents/counselors/1788300021-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:23:- `SchwabToken.current` (latest row). Predicates: `access_expired?`, `refresh_expired?`, `refresh_expiring_within?(24.hours)`, `usable?`. `SchwabToken.issue!(token_response)` on code exchange: new row, `issued_at` now, `refresh_expires_at` = issued_at + 7 days. `SchwabToken#refresh!`: calls the client's refresh grant under a row lock so two jobs cannot double-refresh; updates access token and `access_expires_at`, stores whatever refresh_token comes back, never touches `refresh_expires_at`; on `ReauthRequired` records `last_refresh_error`, audits `token_refresh_failed`, and pauses sync via `system_settings.sync_paused_reason`.
agents/counselors/1788300021-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:25:- `Schwab::TokenHealthJob` daily 08:00 and 20:00 ET: nag email when `refresh_expires_at` < now + 24h; on Monday and Tuesday also nag if `refresh_expires_at` is before the coming Sunday 18:00 email plus 12h buffer; audits `token_nag_sent`.
agents/counselors/1788298125-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:5:This is the biggest auth flaw. Mail scanners, link previewers, safe-browsing systems, and `HEAD`/`GET` prefetches can trigger `magic`, update `last_login_at`, create a session for the scanner response, and burn the user’s link before the user clicks. For this app, make the emailed URL a non-mutating landing page. Require an explicit same-site `POST` with CSRF to consume the token and create the session.
agents/counselors/1788298125-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:17:`:token` is filtered as a parameter, but the bearer token is in the path: `/session/magic/:token`. Rails logs, reverse-proxy logs, browser history, mail security systems, and observability tools commonly retain paths. Move the token out of the path at minimum, and explicitly configure app/proxy logging to avoid recording magic-link URLs. The better fix is a short-lived, non-mutating landing URL plus POST consumption.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/codex-5.5-high.md:3:No. [docs/phase-1-plan.md](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/phase-1-plan.md:1) is broadly aligned with Phase 1, but it is not yet a faithful or complete implementation plan. The biggest problems are journal correctness, stop/open-risk semantics, token gating for scheduled runs, and several schema choices that will likely need Phase 2 rework.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/codex-5.5-high.md:7:1. **Open risk is incorrectly treated as zero in Phase 1.**  
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/codex-5.5-high.md:8:   The plan says working stop/distance-to-stop are `nil` and open risk is `0` until stops exist in app-created proposals: [phase-1-plan.md:40](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/phase-1-plan.md:40), [phase-1-plan.md:82](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/phase-1-plan.md:82). That contradicts the PRD/UI requirement that dashboard and briefs surface distance to stop and open risk: [prd.md:141](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:141), [ui-flows.md:38](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:38).  
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/codex-5.5-high.md:9:   Absence of a stop is not zero risk. It is unknown/unprotected risk. Phase 1 syncs Schwab orders, so it should detect broker-side stop orders where present and flag `unprotected` where absent.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/codex-5.5-high.md:11:2. **The journal builder cannot handle existing positions or sell-first histories.**  
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/codex-5.5-high.md:12:   The algorithm only opens a trade when there is no open trade and a buy fill arrives: [phase-1-plan.md:100](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/phase-1-plan.md:100). That fails the day-one reality: the account may already hold positions, and the first synced fill may be a sell/scale-out. The PRD’s zero-to-zero lifecycle model needs a legacy/open-incomplete path for positions whose entry history predates sync. Otherwise Phase 1 will silently mis-journal real exits.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/codex-5.5-high.md:15:   The plan uses `open`, `closed`, `incomplete`: [phase-1-plan.md:37](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/phase-1-plan.md:37). But an orphan trade can be open or closed while still incomplete. This enum will be undone in Phase 2. Use separate fields: lifecycle status (`open`/`closed`) plus completion fields such as `setup_id`, `planned_stop`, `journal_completed_at`, or `needs_review`.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/codex-5.5-high.md:18:   The plan says incomplete trades can be completed from Flow 4, but only includes post-mortem and followed/improvised: [phase-1-plan.md:116](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/phase-1-plan.md:116). The PRD says orphan fills need missing stop/setup captured: [prd.md:75](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:75). Add an incomplete-fill review path with setup and planned stop, matching the UI addendum’s orphan-fill review direction: [ui-flows.md:172](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-ui-flows.md:172).
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/codex-5.5-high.md:21:   The PRD says all scheduled work checks token health and queues/degrades rather than silently skipping: [prd.md:61](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:61). The plan only applies `TokenGated` to Schwab-touching jobs: [phase-1-plan.md:55](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/phase-1-plan.md:55). Morning/EOD agent runs also depend on fresh synced data and tools that may call Schwab. They need explicit gating behavior: queue, send degraded health-only email, or run against stale data with a prominent stale-data mode.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/codex-5.5-high.md:25:6. **`transactions` lacks an order link, but the journal depends on one.**  
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/codex-5.5-high.md:26:   The journal says it copies setup/thesis/planned stop if a fill’s order maps to a proposal: [phase-1-plan.md:101](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/phase-1-plan.md:101). The transaction schema has no `order_id`, `broker_order_id`, or execution/order reference: [phase-1-plan.md:35](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/phase-1-plan.md:35). Do not rely on `raw` for this contract. Add explicit nullable linkage.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/codex-5.5-high.md:38:   Phase 1 tools are all read-only, so the plan works today: [phase-1-plan.md:78](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/phase-1-plan.md:78). But PRD §5.5a requires one internal tool surface with scheduled runs read-only forever: [prd.md:159](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:159). Add tool metadata like `read_only`, `interactive_allowed`, `scheduled_allowed` now so Phase 2 write tools cannot accidentally enter unattended runs.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/codex-5.5-high.md:42:- `evaluate_hypothetical_order` omission is correct for Phase 1 because guardrails are Phase 2, but the plan contradicts itself: resolved in decision 0.5, then “pending decision 0.5”: [phase-1-plan.md:15](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/phase-1-plan.md:15), [phase-1-plan.md:90](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/phase-1-plan.md:90). Clean that up.
agents/counselors/1788296923-review-request-question-is-docsphase-1/codex-5.5-high.md:56:The plan is a strong scaffold, but not ready to build from. Fix stop/open-risk semantics, split trade lifecycle from journal completeness, add explicit transaction-order linkage, gate scheduled runs, and harden snapshot/account modeling before migrations are written.
agents/counselors/1788298377-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:7:Before build step 3 (the Schwab adapter) is written, produce the best-available contract for each Schwab Trader API and Market Data API call Phase 1 needs, and critique the plan's adapter design. The app has no API access yet, so the adapter will be built from community knowledge (schwab-py, schwab-api community clients, the api-evangelist OpenAPI skeletons) and every shape assumption is marked `# SCHWAB_SHAPE_UNVERIFIED` until official access arrives.
agents/counselors/1788298377-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:12:- @docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md §5.1, §5.3, §7, §9
agents/counselors/1788298377-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:17:`Schwab::Client` (Net::HTTP, no Faraday) with an OAuth module (authorize URL, code exchange, refresh grant), retry with exponential backoff on 429/5xx honoring Retry-After (max 3 attempts), a per-process token bucket at 120 requests/minute, request logging of method/path/status/duration only. Endpoint methods: `account_numbers`, `accounts(fields: :positions)`, `account(hash, fields:)`, `orders(hash, from:, to:, status:)`, `transactions(hash, from:, to:, types:)`, `market_hours(markets:, date:)`, `quotes(symbols)`, `price_history(symbol, period_type:, period:, frequency_type:, frequency:)`. Response mappers live beside the client and are the only code that touches Schwab field names. `Schwab::FakeClient` mirrors the interface for dev seeds and Playwright.
agents/counselors/1788298377-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:22:1. For each call above, give: HTTP method and path on `api.schwabapi.com`, required headers, query parameters with formats (date/time formats matter), and the response shape down to the field names Phase 1 needs: account hashValue and accountNumber pairing; positions with instrument cusip/symbol/assetType/instrumentId, longQuantity/shortQuantity, averagePrice, marketValue; currentBalances fields relevant to settled vs unsettled cash for a cash account; order fields (orderId, status, orderType, session, duration, orderStrategyType, childOrderStrategies, replacingOrderCollection, orderLegCollection with instruction/quantity/instrument, stopPrice, price, enteredTime, closeTime, filledQuantity); transaction/activity fields (activityId, type, subAccount, tradeDate, settlementDate, orderId, netAmount, transferItems with instrument/amount/cost/price/feeType/positionEffect); market hours (per-market sessionHours with preMarket/regularMarket/postMarket start and end, isOpen); quote fields; price history candles.
agents/counselors/1788298377-review-request-question-before-build-st/prompt.md:27:6. Then critique the adapter design: interface shape, error taxonomy (auth failure vs rate limit vs server error vs unknown-outcome must be distinguishable by callers), what the FakeClient must be able to script for Playwright (re-auth success and failure at minimum), and how mappers should handle missing CUSIPs and unknown enum values without crashing sync.
agents/counselors/1788298377-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:107:Response is an array of orders. Fields Phase 1 needs:
agents/counselors/1788298377-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:160:  "user": { "cdDomainId", "login", "type", "userId", "systemUserName", "firstName", "lastName", "brokerRepCode" },  // drop
agents/counselors/1788298377-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:274:- Whether `/trader/v1/userPreference` returns a per-account `nickName` usable for the dashboard label (it also carries plaintext numbers, so scrub).
agents/counselors/1788298377-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:278:**Put the FakeClient below the mappers, not above them.** If `Schwab::FakeClient` returns mapped structs, seeds and Playwright never exercise the mapping code, which is where every shape assumption lives. Have both clients return scrubbed raw hashes with the same shape and run both through the same mappers. The fixtures the FakeClient serves are then also the VCR-shaped fixtures for specs, one set of `# SCHWAB_SHAPE_UNVERIFIED` payloads instead of two.
agents/counselors/1788298377-review-request-question-before-build-st/claude-fable.md:302:**FakeClient scenarios Playwright and seeds need.** Scripted per call through the `/playwright/scenarios/:name` route: re-auth success (fake authorize page redirects to `/schwab/callback?code=FAKE%40&state=...`), re-auth failure (`invalid_grant`), refresh expired (`ReauthRequired`), rate limited then success, server error then success, transport timeout, empty account, position removed between two syncs, order with nested bracket child, transaction with missing CUSIP, unknown enum value, closed market day, quotes batch with one invalid symbol, and the four dashboard banner states. Each scenario is a named fixture set plus an optional per-call response queue, so a test can say "first `orders` call raises RateLimited, second succeeds."
agents/counselors/1788299995-review-request-question-review-build-st/prompt.md:7:Review build step 3 of Phase 1: the Schwab adapter layer (HTTP client, OAuth calls, error taxonomy, scrubbing, rate budget, typed mappers, fake client, fixtures). Check it against the contract it was built to, and look for bugs that would only show up against the real API or under concurrency.
agents/counselors/1788298125-review-request-question-review-build-st/prompt.md:7:Review build step 1 of Phase 1 (tooling, passwordless magic-link authentication, credentials layout, mail config, CI pipeline, app shell) for correctness, security, and idiomatic Rails 8.1. This is a single-operator finance app that will hold Schwab OAuth tokens, so authentication mistakes matter more than usual.
agents/counselors/1788298125-review-request-question-review-build-st/prompt.md:17:- @spec/models/user_spec.rb, @spec/requests/sessions_spec.rb, @spec/requests/dashboard_spec.rb, @spec/mailers/magic_link_mailer_spec.rb, @spec/tasks/login_spec.rb
agents/counselors/1788302335-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:9:**1. A non-Schwab exception or a worker restart freezes a feed forever.** `SyncRun.record` at `app/models/sync_run.rb:16` rescues only `Schwab::Error`. Anything else propagates and leaves the row `status: running` with no `finished_at`. `SyncRun.due?` at `app/models/sync_run.rb:31` returns false while any running row exists, with no age bound. So one `ActiveRecord::NotNullViolation` (an order without `status`), one `RecordInvalid`, one `RecordNotUnique` on the positions index, or a dokku deploy that restarts `bin/jobs` mid-run stops that feed and account from ever being scheduled again. The tick reports nothing; the dashboard just goes stale. Deploys alone guarantee this happens. Fix: `ensure` in `record` that finishes `:failed` when the row is still running (re-raise after), and make `running?` ignore rows older than a bound (10 minutes covers the slowest feed here). Add `retry_on`/`discard_on` policy to the feed jobs so Solid Queue does not also retry a poisoned run.
agents/counselors/1788302335-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:19:**5. An `AWAITING_PARENT_ORDER` child counts as protection.** `Position#protection` at `app/models/position.rb:16` accepts any working status. The preference in `assign_working_stop!` only matters when a live stop also exists. Hold 40 shares with no stop, place a 40-share bracket, and the dashboard says protected while the child is not in the market. Return a distinct unprotected reason for a stop whose status is awaiting its parent.
agents/counselors/1788302335-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:22:- Any TRADE whose security is not EQUITY becomes `sweep`. The contract lists `COLLECTIVE_INVESTMENT` and `MUTUAL_FUND`, so an ETF or fund fill is filed as a sweep and never journaled. Only `CASH_EQUIVALENT` is a sweep; everything else with a security is a fill.
agents/counselors/1788302335-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:24:- A money-market dividend on SWVXX is `dividend`, not `interest`. Harmless for the journal, wrong for reporting.
agents/counselors/1788302335-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:28:**8. `pause!` can leave a stale pause reason.** `app/jobs/sync/tick_job.rb:31` is a check-then-write with no lock. `issue!` clears the reason under the settings row lock; the tick can read nil, lose the race, and write the reason after the new token is current. Sync runs, but the dashboard says paused until the next re-auth. Take the same lock and re-check `SchwabToken.usable?` inside it.
agents/counselors/1788302335-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:37:- The `other` quarantine and the gap audit fire on every run for as long as the record or stale cursor sits in the window: partial runs for 59 days and an audit row per run. Quarantine on `new_record?` only, and audit the gap once per `gap_from`.
agents/counselors/1788302335-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:43:**Missing specs.** A non-Schwab exception inside `record`. A stale running row and the tick. The resolve collision after a successful CUSIP lookup (add SWVXX to `instruments.json` and the feeds spec hangs today). A bad order and a bad activity mid-batch. Refetch 404 clearing a stop. Awaiting-child protection. Scale-in coverage. ETF and fee-only classification. Working pass count. Catch-up overlapping a tick. The pause and issue race.
agents/counselors/1788301084-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:10:2. **Critical: stale refresh can still pause sync after a newer re-auth.**  
agents/counselors/1788301084-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:24:The Monday/Tuesday rule is now the right shape: Sunday 18:30 re-auth stays quiet Monday 08:00; Wednesday re-auth nags next Monday; Sunday 17:00 nags because it was before the 18:00 ritual; DST is handled by constructing Sunday 18:00 in `America/New_York`.
agents/counselors/1788301084-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:30:Add real-adapter request/model specs for OAuth with no current token, a true race around `record_failure`, parser checks for `config/recurring.yml`, DST/Sunday-17 health cases, and log/error scrubbing. The current refresh race spec is sequential and does not prove the stale-row pause race is closed.
agents/counselors/1788300021-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:3:The planned step 4 is close on the happy path, but it is not operationally safe yet. The main failure mode is not just “token expires”; it is “an old token actor changes global system state after a newer re-auth succeeded.” That can silently pause automation even though the user did the right thing.
agents/counselors/1788300021-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:9:A refresh job may load token row A, then the user completes re-auth and `issue!` creates token row B. If the old refresh later receives a token-endpoint 4xx, the planned `refresh!` pauses sync globally via `system_settings.sync_paused_reason`.
agents/counselors/1788300021-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:23:A row lock is necessary but not sufficient. If two jobs enter, the second must reload inside the lock and skip if the first already refreshed recently. Otherwise it may immediately reuse the newly returned refresh token or, worse, a stale token captured before the lock.
agents/counselors/1788300021-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:33:The phase plan says Monday/Tuesday nag if `refresh_expires_at` is before the coming Sunday 18:00 email plus 12h buffer. A token issued Sunday evening can never survive until the following Monday 06:00, so this rule will nag even after a successful Sunday re-auth.
agents/counselors/1788300021-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:35:This conflicts with the PRD’s Sunday ritual in [investment-copilot-prd.md](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:211).
agents/counselors/1788300021-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:37:Required fix: define escalation in terms of whether the last Sunday ritual was completed, not whether the token survives past next Sunday plus 12h. For example:
agents/counselors/1788300021-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:38:- Sunday email always includes re-auth.
agents/counselors/1788300021-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:76:- Agent jobs: run degraded with stale timestamps.
agents/counselors/1788300021-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:103:- Prevent stale in-flight jobs using an old token from pausing or mutating submission state after re-auth.
agents/counselors/1788300021-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:114:- Monday after successful Sunday re-auth does not nag.
agents/counselors/1788300021-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:115:- Monday after missed Sunday ritual does nag.
agents/counselors/1788302335-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:15:7. **High: journaling handoffs are missing, and nil status is treated as journalable.** The design says positions enqueue bootstrap and activities enqueue fill-linking; there are no `Journal::*` jobs referenced from [PositionsJob](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/jobs/sync/positions_job.rb:26) or [ActivitiesJob](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/jobs/sync/activities_job.rb:34). Also [valid_for_journal](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/activity.rb:14) includes `nil`; the rule is only `VALID` journals.
agents/counselors/1788302335-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:19:9. **Medium: positions omit cost basis.** [PositionsJob](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/jobs/sync/positions_job.rb:20) writes quantity, average price, market value, and last price, but never `cost_basis`. [Schwab::Position](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/schwab/position.rb:3) also does not parse it. This loses a Phase 1 column on every real sync.
agents/counselors/1788302335-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:21:10. **Medium: proactive token refresh is not wired.** [Schwab.client](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/schwab.rb:15) passes `usable_token!` directly; [ensure_fresh!](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/schwab_token.rb:59) is never called there. The system will rely on 401 refreshes instead of refreshing ahead as designed.
agents/counselors/1788302335-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:29:The fixes are directionally better than the earlier design, but this is not ready for a real Schwab account. The biggest remaining risks are stale `running` rows, duplicate queue growth, incomplete orders changing stop protection, old GTC stops missed on first sync, and activity cursor loss across per-type failures. I did not run the test suite; this was a static review against the code and specs.
agents/counselors/1788301121-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:14:   “Newest working SELL stop on same account/instrument with stop price” is not enough. It will mishandle bracket children in `AWAITING_PARENT_ORDER`, replaced stops, partial fills, oversized stops, and stale cancel/replace chains. Detection needs:
agents/counselors/1788301121-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:36:   The PRD says market hours derive from Schwab and nothing hardcodes 9:30-16:00 ([PRD](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/docs/artifacts/investment-copilot-prd.md:87)). A weekday 9:30-16:00 fallback will be wrong on holidays and early closes. Prefer last-known Schwab calendar with stale marking. If there is no Schwab-backed row, fallback may drive low-stakes cadence only, not snapshots, market-day briefs, or “regular close + 20 min” decisions.
agents/counselors/1788301121-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:44:   Cash-account reality includes money-market sweeps, journal transfers, interest, fees, and corrections. If these collapse into `other`, snapshots and flow-adjusted drawdown become wrong. Every `other` should increment `unmapped_values` with raw `type`, `description`, `subAccount`, sign, and transfer item shape. Cash-affecting `other` should be a partial run, not a quiet success.
agents/counselors/1788301121-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:66:- Calendar fallback is stale/degraded data, not authoritative market-hours truth.
agents/counselors/1788298377-review-request-question-before-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:37:Cash balances under `currentBalances`: Phase 1 needs `cashAvailableForTrading`, `cashAvailableForWithdrawal`, `cashBalance`, `totalCash`, `unsettledCash`, and probably `longNonMarginableMarketValue`. For equity use `liquidationValue` if present, else cash plus position market value. `settled_cash` should not be derived casually; conservative v1 mapping is `cashAvailableForTrading` as spendable cash, `unsettledCash` as separate warning field. ([docs.rs](https://docs.rs/schwab/latest/schwab/struct.CashBalance.html)) `# SCHWAB_SHAPE_UNVERIFIED: exact settled-cash source field for cash accounts`.
agents/counselors/1788302335-review-request-question-review-build-st/prompt.md:7:Review build step 5 of Phase 1: the Schwab sync layer (sync-run bookkeeping, market calendar, instrument resolution, working-stop detection, the accounts/positions/orders/activities feeds, the tick scheduler, catch-up). It was built to the design you reviewed; verify the fixes hold against the code and find what will still go wrong on a real account.
agents/counselors/1788302335-review-request-question-review-build-st/prompt.md:31:- Check ActivitiesJob's per-type error handling and cursor semantics; check the kind classification against a cash account's real activity (sweeps, journals, fees, interest); check that non-VALID activities are stored but excluded from journaling
agents/counselors/1788298853-review-request-question-review-build-st/prompt.md:7:Review build step 2 of Phase 1: the complete data model (21 tables) for the Investment Copilot, implemented as migrations and Active Record models with model specs. Check it against the plan and the PRD, and against what Phase 2 will need, since the point of shipping every table now is that Phase 2 never alters one.
