agents/counselors/1788298853-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:11:3. **No uniqueness on open trades.** `db/migrate/20260901220010_create_trades.rb:28` is a plain composite index. `Journal::BootstrapJob` runs after every positions sync and `Journal::LinkFillsJob` after every transactions sync, from different tick cadences, and both create trades. Without a partial unique index the journal silently forks. This is the trades equivalent of the `trade_legs.transaction_id` index:
agents/counselors/1788298853-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:24:6. **`SystemSettings.instance` races.** `app/models/system_settings.rb:7` does `first || create!`; the tick job and a web request against an empty table can produce two rows. Add `t.check_constraint "id = 1"` and use `find_or_create_by!(id: 1)`. Drop `self.table_name`; Rails already infers it.
agents/counselors/1788298853-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:26:7. **`accounts.account_type` NOT NULL with no source.** Schwab's `/accounts` returns CASH or MARGIN, not taxable or ira, so `Sync::AccountsJob` will have nothing to write and the upsert fails. Make it nullable, meaning unclassified until set on the system screen, with `trading_enabled` already defaulting false. Also `accounts` is the only synced table without `raw` jsonb. `db/migrate/20260901220001_create_accounts.rb`.
agents/counselors/1788298853-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:34:11. **Destructive `dependent` options.** `app/models/account.rb:2-8` destroys positions, orders, transactions, trades, snapshots on `account.destroy`. Accounts are never deleted; use `restrict_with_exception` like `Instrument`. `app/models/setup.rb:2` nullifies `trades.setup_id` on delete, which strips journal tags; setups have `active` for retirement, so restrict there too.
agents/counselors/1788298853-review-request-question-review-build-st/claude-fable.md:43:- **trades / trade_legs:** the open-trade index above. Consider `trades.quantity` for the running open quantity; plan §4 recomputes it from legs, and with split ratios that fold runs on every `get_journal` call.
agents/counselors/1788298853-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:13:   [app/models/account.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/account.rb:2) uses `dependent: :destroy` for positions, balances, orders, transactions, trades, snapshots, and proposals. [app/models/order_proposal.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/app/models/order_proposal.rb:7) can nullify orders and destroy submission attempts. That is wrong for broker history, journal history, and duplicate-submission forensics. Prefer `restrict_with_exception` for accounts/proposals once rows have historical meaning.
agents/counselors/1788298853-review-request-question-review-build-st/codex-5.5-high.md:16:   The journal builder is zero-to-zero, one open lifecycle per account/instrument. Current schema only has a non-unique index on `[account_id, instrument_id, status]` in [db/migrate/20260901220010_create_trades.rb](/Users/jathayde/Development/Personal/desk.athayde/db/migrate/20260901220010_create_trades.rb:28). Concurrent bootstrap/link jobs can create duplicate open trades. Add a partial unique index on `(account_id, instrument_id)` where `status = 'open'`.

